// The environment variables Jet's tools, generated programs and repository
// verification read: the one hand-written home of their names. Each row names
// the repository file that reads the variable, the value it accepts and what
// it means. `Tools/agent/EnvironmentRows.jet` renders the tables of
// Docs/spec/reference/environment.md from these rows, and the names code
// spells them by: an `ENV_<VARIABLE>` constant (EnvironmentNames.jet beside
// this file, and the test kit's copy in JetTestKit EnvironmentNames.jet) and
// the runtime's `env_name_<variable>` accessor (JetRuntime
// EnvironmentNames.jet). tests/guards/environment_variables.jet fails on a
// `JET_*` or `JETPACK_*` literal in the compiler with no row, and on a row
// whose reader no longer names it. A compiler control's variable is a row of
// JET_CLI_CONTROLS (CLIControls.jet), not of this table.

// Who sets a variable: a user or automation, a maintainer or CI run, or a
// Jet-owned process handing state to a child (no compatibility promise).
JetEnvironmentSection: enum {
    User Maintainer Internal
}

// One variable. A `name` ending in `*` is a family: every variable whose name
// starts with the text before the `*`. `reader` is a repository path whose
// text names the variable (a family: its prefix). `value` is empty for an
// internal row.
JetEnvironmentVariable: struct {
    name: String
    section: JetEnvironmentSection
    reader: String
    value: String
    meaning: String
}

JET_ENVIRONMENT_VARIABLES: [JetEnvironmentVariable]{
    {name: "JETPACK_BIN", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/InspectB.jet", value: "executable path", meaning: "Names the `jetpack` engine that `jet`'s engine verbs (`fetch`, `add`, `env`, `trust`, …) run. The lookup order is `JETPACK_BIN`, then the `jetpack` beside the running `jet`, then `PATH`; a `JETPACK_BIN` that names no executable file refuses with E1228 instead of falling through. `jet test --jetpack=<path>` (the `jetpack` test setting) sets it for every corpus row it runs, which otherwise get the engine this order finds for the jet under test. The name predates the `JET_<AREA>_<SETTING>` convention; it matches the `JETPACK_BIN` that Jetpack's process claims already use."},
    {name: "JETPACK_DENY_NETWORK", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Provider/Source/Core/HardenedCommands.jet", value: "any non-empty value", meaning: "Keeps `jetpack` off the network: a provider fetch, a source-channel refresh, a toolchain update or a pinned-bubblewrap download fails as offline instead."},
    {name: "JETPACK_HANGAR_MAX_BYTES", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Store/Source/Hangar/AdmissionQuota.jet", value: "positive byte count", meaning: "The Hangar's largest size (128 GiB when unset). It wins over the Hangar's `config/hangar-max-bytes`."},
    {name: "JETPACK_NIX_FALLBACK_BIN", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Nix/Source/Fallback/FallbackPolicy.jet", value: "executable path", meaning: "Names the Nix a local Nix fallback runs, instead of the one on `PATH`."},
    {name: "JETPACK_NIX_FALLBACK_POLICY", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Nix/Source/Fallback/FallbackPolicy.jet", value: "`allow` or `deny`", meaning: "`allow` lets a CI or non-interactive run fall back to a local Nix; `deny` forbids the fallback everywhere. Unset, only an interactive run falls back."},
    {name: "JETPACK_PRINCIPAL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Hangar/ExternalRootCommands.jet", value: "principal name", meaning: "The principal recorded on a manually registered external root, instead of the CLI's."},
    {name: "JETPACK_SHARED_CAS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Store/HangarRoots.jet", value: "directory", meaning: "Names the content-addressed store every Hangar root shares, instead of each root's own `cas` directory."},
    {name: "JETPACK_SHELL_ON_FAIL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Commands/DiscoveryCommands.jet", value: "shell executable", meaning: "The shell a failed build opens in its preserved scratch directory, instead of `SHELL` (else `sh`, or `cmd` on Windows)."},
    {name: "JET_ADVISORY_DB", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Publication/Source/Advisory.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Names the advisory database a lock is checked against, instead of the project's `.jet/advisories.db`."},
    {name: "JET_BUILD_TARGET", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Integrations/Source/Foreign/RustBridge/NativeToolchain.jet", value: "target triple", meaning: "The target triple a Rust FFI bridge builds for, instead of rustc's host."},
    {name: "JET_BWRAP_URL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Foundation/Source/NativeSandbox.jet", value: "`https://` or `file://` URL", meaning: "Names where a command that runs build actions (`jet build`, `jet cc`) fetches Jet's pinned bubblewrap when neither the `bwrap` on PATH nor a pinned copy in the Hangar (`<hangar>/tools/<sha256>/bwrap`) or beside jet passes its probe, instead of the jet release. The file must still hash to the SHA-256 jet embeds (`NATIVE_SANDBOX_BWRAP_ASSETS`); a `file://` copy works offline, and `JETPACK_DENY_NETWORK` refuses an `https://` fetch."},
    {name: "JET_CC_PACK_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/ForeignLink.jet", value: "directory", meaning: "Names an unpacked C toolchain pack (a `jet env fetch-toolchain --json` root) whose clang and llvm-ar build a C or C++ file with `jet run` and `jet build` on every tier, instead of the pack jet's `jetpack` fetches. A Jet program's C closure still takes the pack and its musl sysroot from the `jetpack` engine. `CC` or `AR` still win. A golden `jet test` run with a jetpack sets it for every row."},
    {name: "JET_CC_PACK_URL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Provider/Source/Toolchain/CcToolchainPack.jet", value: "`https://` or `file://` URL", meaning: "Names where `jet cc` and `jet env fetch-toolchain` fetch this jet's C toolchain pack when it is neither in the Hangar nor beside jet, instead of the jet release. The pack must still hash to the SHA-256 jet embeds; a `file://` pack is a local copy and works offline."},
    {name: "JET_ENV_DISABLE", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetFoundation/Data/Syntax/EffectsSurface.jet", value: "any non-empty value", meaning: "The escape for `jet env hook`; suppresses automatic activation in the current shell and drops environment that hook already activated."},
    {name: "JET_FFI_CACHE_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/RustForeign.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the hidden Rust FFI bridge cache directory."},
    {name: "JET_FUZZ_ITERATIONS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "positive integer", meaning: "Sets the generated fuzz-case limit: the cases each property test runs (200 when unset). `jet test --grade=generated --iterations=<n>` sets it on the test harness (1000 when `--iterations` is unset)."},
    {name: "JET_HELP_SHELL_PREFILL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Picker.jet", value: "any value", meaning: "Set by the `jet env hook` and branded-shell widgets (bare `jet`, Alt-?) when they run bare `jet` with stdout captured: the command picker still opens while stdin and stderr are a terminal, and prints the picked command line on stdout for the shell to put in its edit buffer, never running it. Unset, a picked line is only named on stderr."},
    {name: "JET_INSPECT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Manifest/ReleaseDevtools.jet", value: "`1`", meaning: "Turns on a release deployment's devtools inspection."},
    {name: "JET_INSPECT_ALLOWLIST", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Manifest/ReleaseDevtools.jet", value: "comma-separated networks", meaning: "The networks (at most 64) a release deployment's devtools inspection answers."},
    {name: "JET_INSPECT_TOKEN", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Manifest/ReleaseDevtools.jet", value: "token", meaning: "The token a release deployment's devtools inspection requires."},
    {name: "JET_KEYS_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Doctor/HealthReport.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the signing-key directory used by publishing and secrets tooling."},
    {name: "JET_PACKAGE_STORE_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Store/SourceStore.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the package-store directory."},
    {name: "JET_PROP_SEED", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "integer from 0 to 2^63-1", meaning: "Replays a property-test run with the seed its failure report printed. `jet test --grade=generated --seed=<n>` sets it on the test harness (the fixed 0 when `--seed` is unset and the caller sets none). `jet prove` runs every property from this seed, else from one derived from the program's inputs, and names it in each property row as `effectiveSeed`."},
    {name: "JET_REGISTRY_*", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Registry/RegistryIdentity.jet", value: "URL, or `true`", meaning: "`JET_REGISTRY_<NAME>_URL` names the endpoint of the registry `<name>` (in lowercase); `JET_REGISTRY_<NAME>_MIRROR=true` marks that registry a mirror. No Git that `jetpack` runs sees a `JET_REGISTRY_` variable."},
    {name: "JET_REGISTRY_CACHE_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Publication/Source/Registry/Cache.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the local registry-index cache."},
    {name: "JET_REGISTRY_NAME", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Doctor/HealthReport.jet", value: "registry name", meaning: "Selects the named registry used by Jetpack doctor checks."},
    {name: "JET_REGISTRY_ROOT_KEY", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Publication/Source/Registry/Trust.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Names the pinned registry root key, instead of the registry's own key path. A configured key that is missing refuses."},
    {name: "JET_REGISTRY_TIER", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/PackageModel/Source/Registry/RegistryIdentity.jet", value: "`core`, `community`, …", meaning: "Selects the publication registry tier (`core` when unset or unknown)."},
    {name: "JET_REGISTRY_URL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Doctor/HealthReport.jet", value: "URL", meaning: "Overrides the default registry index."},
    {name: "JET_REPL_HISTORY", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetTestKit/Source/Exec.jet", value: "`off`", meaning: "Keeps REPL history in memory for the current session instead of persisting it."},
    {name: "JET_REPL_HISTORY_LIMIT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "tests/cases/repl/repl_history_limit_and_corrupt_tail_recover_visibly.case", value: "positive integer", meaning: "Sets the maximum persisted REPL entries."},
    {name: "JET_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Core/Time/Time.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the installed Jet runtime-data root."},
    {name: "JET_SCHEDULER_THREADS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetRuntime/Source/SchedulerMessages.jet", value: "positive integer", meaning: "Sets the generated program's scheduler worker count."},
    {name: "JET_TARGET", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Env/ComposeEnv.jet", value: "target triple", meaning: "The target an environment's task facts, its entry receipt and a foreign bridge record, instead of the host's."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_FILTER", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "test-name substring", meaning: "Selects generated `jet test` cases; prefer the corresponding CLI flag."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_SERIAL", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "`1`", meaning: "Runs generated `jet test` cases serially; prefer the corresponding CLI flag."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_SHUFFLE_SEED", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "unsigned integer", meaning: "Replays a shuffled generated test run."},
    {name: "JET_TOOLCHAIN_ENDPOINT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Jetpack/Recipe/Source/Toolchain/ChannelManifest.jet", value: "URL", meaning: "Names the toolchain update endpoint, instead of the project's configured one and `https://dl.jet-lang.dev`."},
    {name: "JET_TZDB_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.User, reader: "Core/Time/Time.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the timezone database read by generated programs."},
    {name: "JETPACK_SEAL_CENSUS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Jetpack/Store/Source/Seal/SealRecord.jet", value: "any value", meaning: "Counts how often each path is sealed and reports the census."},
    {name: "JETPACK_TIMING", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Jetpack/CLI/Source/Env/ComposeEnv.jet", value: "any value", meaning: "Reports the time each phase of composing an environment took."},
    {name: "JETPACK_VERIFY_TRACE", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Jetpack/Store/Source/Reuse/VerifiedReuse.jet", value: "any value", meaning: "Prints to stderr why each cache entry failed verification."},
    {name: "JET_BASE_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the published compilers. Unset, `$JET_SCRATCH_ROOT/discovery/base`."},
    {name: "JET_CFFI_ABI", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "tests/cases/cffi_native_matrix/required_native_c_abi_matrix_default.case", value: "ABI name", meaning: "Selects the C-ABI matrix row. Companion `JET_CFFI_CC`, `JET_CFFI_AR`, `JET_CFFI_RUST_TARGET`, `JET_CFFI_RUST_LINKER`, and `JET_CFFI_RUNNER` name that row's tools and target."},
    {name: "JET_CHECK_MEM", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet", value: "a size such as `20G`, `512M` or `4096K`, or `off`", meaning: "The address-space cap of each compiler check `Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet` runs; `off` runs it uncapped. Unset, `20G`."},
    {name: "JET_CHECK_SLOTS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet", value: "count", meaning: "How many compiler checks of `Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet` run at once on the machine; the rest wait for a slot. Unset, 2."},
    {name: "JET_CLI_FMT_TEST_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Tests/ExternalFormat.jet", value: "path", meaning: "The directory the JetCli external-format test keeps its fixture under; `Tools/agent/CompilerRegistries.jet` sets it to its scratch. Unset, a fresh temporary directory."},
    {name: "JET_CLOSEOUT_MILESTONE", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/CloseoutGate.jet", value: "milestone", meaning: "The milestone `jet Tools/agent/CloseoutGate.jet check` checks when its command line names none."},
    {name: "JET_COMPILER_IDENTITY", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Request.jet", value: "`name@version#build-id`", meaning: "Names the running compiler's identity, which keys its receipts and versions its target layout. Unset, `jet` reads the one line of the `IDENTITY` file beside its executable; with neither, every compile refuses (E2105) and names both. A code suite of `jet test` (the `packages`, `selfhost` and `perf` profiles of `Compiler`) gets the identity of the jet under test here, so it runs in a shell that sets none."},
    {name: "JET_DEV_WORKTREE", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the checkout the lander commits to. Unset, the checkout holding the tool."},
    {name: "JET_FRONT_TIMEOUT_MS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/CompilerRegistries.jet", value: "milliseconds", meaning: "The timeout of each front-end command a compiler registry transport runs. Unset, 600000."},
    {name: "JET_MIN_FREE_MB", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet", value: "megabytes", meaning: "The available memory a compiler check of `Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet` waits for before it starts. Unset, 8000."},
    {name: "JET_ORCHESTRATOR_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Batch10.jet", value: "path", meaning: "The directory the orchestrator's batch tools (`Batch10.jet`, `Integrate10.jet`, `StreamB10.jet`) run `Integrate10.jet` from. Unset, the running tool's own directory."},
    {name: "JET_PERF_MAP", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "`1`", meaning: "**Internal** profiling aid for `jet run` and `jet dev`: before a program runs from memory, jet writes `/tmp/perf-<pid>.map` from its image's symbol table, so `perf report` shows its function names (`Compiler/JetBackend/Source/Image/Loader.jet`, `x64_image_perf_map`). Unset, nothing is written."},
    {name: "JET_READ_SCOPE", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "comma-separated paths", meaning: "**Set by jet** for a program that `jet run --allow='FS.Read(\"<path>\")'`, or the same right in its package's `authority.allow` row, confines to reading those paths: a read the confinement refuses fails with `PermissionDenied`, and its cause names E1803 and these paths (`Compiler/JetRuntime/Source/CompilerFS.jet`). Setting it yourself confines nothing; it only changes that wording."},
    {name: "JET_RECHECK_VERIFY", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Request.jet", value: "`1`", meaning: "**Internal** compiler test switch: each body comptime pass that lands its local values in the bodies holding them, instead of checking the whole program again (`Compiler/JetSema/Source/Sema/Comptime/LocalSplice.jet`), also checks the whole program again, and any difference between the two results stops the compile as an internal compiler problem that names the first differing rows."},
    {name: "JET_RELEASE_WORK", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/release/Admit.jet", value: "path", meaning: "The release train's work root, read by `Tools/release/Admit.jet` and `Tools/agent/Land.jet`; `paused` in it stops new trains. Unset, `$JET_STATE_ROOT/release`."},
    {name: "JET_RUN_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the land queue, locks and slot ledger. Unset, `$JET_SCRATCH_ROOT/run`."},
    {name: "JET_SAFETY_ARTIFACTS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet", value: "path", meaning: "The admitted native artifacts JSON the `safety-gate` row of `Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet` runs the full safety gate against (Docs/spec/safety.md). Unset, the row runs the gate's source leg."},
    {name: "JET_SCRATCH_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the large shared scratch, under which the test kit also keeps its scratch and state. Unset, `$JET_STATE_ROOT`."},
    {name: "JET_SEED", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the admitted seed compiler's directory. Unset, `$JET_SEEDS/current`."},
    {name: "JET_SEEDS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the seed store. Unset, `${{XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}}/jet-seeds`."},
    {name: "JET_STATE_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): per-user dev state and caches. Each root is read from the environment, else from `${{XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}}/jet/env`. Unset, `${{XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}}/jet-dev`."},
    {name: "JET_TARGET_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/orchestrator/Roots.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Checkout tool root (`Tools/agent/roots.sh`): the build target directories. Unset, `$JET_SCRATCH_ROOT/targets`."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_SCRATCH", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet", value: "path", meaning: "The scratch directory of a compiler check of `Tools/agent/LaneCheck.jet`. Unset, `$JET_SCRATCH_ROOT/lane-check`."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_SHARD", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet", value: "index", meaning: "The shard of the native suites `Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet` runs, of `JET_TEST_SHARD_COUNT`. Unset, 0."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_SHARD_COUNT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet", value: "count", meaning: "How many shards `Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet` splits the native suites into. Unset, 1."},
    {name: "JET_TEST_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetTestKit/Source/Exec.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Names the toolchain tree the rows of a corpus suite (`golden`, `run`, `ui`, `ui_lint`, `cases`) read their Core from; the testkit hands it to each row as its `JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT` and passes on no `JET_TEST_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT`. Unset, the rows get the kit's `JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT`, else the nearest tree at or above the kit's directory. The `jet` running the kit still reads `JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT`, so a newer runner can test an older `jet` against that jet's own tree, as the release gate does for the current release (`Tools/release/Admit.jet`)."},
    {name: "JET_TIMING_QUIET", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/perf/frame-time/Main.jet", value: "`1`", meaning: "Says the machine is quiet enough to time: the run is pinned to idle CPUs, isolated ones when the kernel has them. Cases that measure wall time against a fixed limit (`requires: env:JET_TIMING_QUIET=1`), such as the Wayland 1 ms frame-time case, run only under it and skip elsewhere; their correctness twins run in every batch. `jet Tools/perf/frame-time/Main.jet` sets it and pins the run to the kernel's isolated CPUs (`/sys/devices/system/cpu/isolated`) or, when there are none, to the CPUs its `--cpu LIST` names; with neither it exits 2."},
    {name: "JET_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Request.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Names the Jet toolchain source tree, the directory holding `Core/` and `Compiler/Prelude/`, that the Core library bodies are read from. Unset, `jet` uses the nearest directory at or above the input that holds both; with none, it compiles against the Core sources built into it. Checkout tools that read the tree's other files (`jet devtools grammars`, the diagnostic coverage report) refuse (E2105) and name both places."},
    {name: "JET_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "`1`", meaning: "Updates compiler-owned snapshot output in explicitly supported workflows, and the files `core.testing.snap` and `core.testing.golden` compare against (`jet test -u` sets it); review the diff immediately."},
    {name: "JET_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet", value: "milliseconds", meaning: "The timeout of each step `Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet` runs. Unset, 3600000."},
    {name: "JET_VERIFY_TMPDIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Tools/agent/VerifyFull.jet", value: "path", meaning: "Overrides the temporary root used by verification scenarios."},
    {name: "JET_X64_EMIT_LOG", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "comma-separated function names or source path parts (an entry holding `/`)", meaning: "**Internal** check aid of the x86-64 selector: with `JET_X64_EMIT_LOG_REPORT` also set, the native build (`jet build`, `jet run`, `jet test`) keeps an emission log of each named function. The log holds the slot IR the selector consumed, each slot's checked type, and one row per jump, call, memory operand (its base and index registers), division, string copy and inline-asm template the encoder wrote. Each row is attributed to the IR instruction it lowers (`Compiler/JetBackend/Source/X64/Encoder.jet`, `X64Code`). A conditional jump whose taken side ends the program (a numeric or shift stop) is marked `stop`, with the one slot its condition reads when there is one. Each body the optimizer inlined is an `inline <site> <outer site> <function>` line, and a `sites` line names the site of every IR instruction (0: the function's own code). Before the functions, one `field <struct> <offset> <size> <member> <type>` line per stored member of each struct the module laid out names what an offset reaches and the member's checked type. Unset, nothing is logged."},
    {name: "JET_X64_EMIT_LOG_REPORT", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Maintainer, reader: "Compiler/JetCli/Source/Cli/Host.jet", value: "path", meaning: "The file the `JET_X64_EMIT_LOG` log is written to, replaced on every native build. A failed write fails the build."},
    {name: "JETPACK_AUTO_CLEAN_ALWAYS", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Internal, reader: "Jetpack/Store/Source/Lifecycle/GarbageCollection.jet", value: "", meaning: "Test hook: the Hangar's automatic clean runs every time, instead of at most once a day."},
    {name: "JETPACK_BOOTSTRAP_*", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Internal, reader: "Compiler/test.jet", value: "", meaning: "The scratch directory, source root and engine areas the Jetpack bootstrap suite hands `Jetpack/Bootstrap/Assemble.jet`."},
    {name: "JETPACK_ENV", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Internal, reader: "Compiler/JetFoundation/Data/Syntax/JetpackConfig.jet", value: "", meaning: "Marks a shell that `jet env` activated."},
    {name: "JETPACK_ENV_DIR", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Internal, reader: "Compiler/JetFoundation/Data/Syntax/EffectsSurface.jet", value: "", meaning: "The `env.jet` directory `jet env hook` last activated, empty for none; a change from it loads or unloads."},
    {name: "JETPACK_ENV_HASH", section: JetEnvironmentSection.Internal, reader: "Compiler/JetFoundation/Data/Syntax/JetpackConfig.jet", value: "", meaning: "The identity of the environment `jet env hook` activated."},
